% Full group axioms with the much harder conclusion that the
% inverse commutes with its element on a specific term.  This
% is `waldmeister/documents/example.pr`'s conclusion verbatim;
% deriving left-inverse from right-inverse + associativity +
% identity is well beyond what our 256-step KBO-with-mapped-LPO
% setup can prove today.  Expected: TIMEOUT, with the saturation
% accumulating many rules.
NAME            group_commutative_inverse
MODE            PROOF
SORTS           ANY
SIGNATURE       e: -> ANY
                i: ANY -> ANY
                f: ANY ANY -> ANY
                a: -> ANY
ORDERING        LPO
                i > f > e > a
VARIABLES       x,y,z : ANY
EQUATIONS       f(x, e) = x
                f(x, i(x)) = e
                f(f(x, y), z) = f(x, f(y, z))
CONCLUSION      f(a, i(a)) = f(i(a), a)
